# Ironworks Plan & Build (L3–L4)

## L3 — /iron:spec — Spec-Driven Development

Every feature starts as a spec before it becomes code.

### Lifecycle

| Phase | Command | Action |
|-------|---------|--------|
| Research | `explore <topic>` | Investigate, update CONTEXT.md |
| Draft | `propose <name>` | RFC-style spec with acceptance criteria |
| Build | `apply <spec>` | Implement, link changes to requirements |
| Check | `verify <spec>` | Validate impl matches spec |
| Revise | `update <name>` | Modify spec with delta markers |
| Complete | `archive <spec>` | Move to archive |

### Spec Format

- **GIVEN/WHEN/THEN** acceptance criteria for every requirement
- **RFC 2119 keywords**: MUST, SHOULD, MAY used precisely
- Delta markers track changes: `[+]` added, `[-]` removed, `[~]` modified

### Rules

- Every feature traces to a spec
- Code without a spec is unauthorized code
- Specs live in `ironworks/specs/`

